# Repos the e2e suite needs checked out BESIDE it on the CI venue.
#
# Declaring a sibling here is what makes its cross-repo guards actually run. An
# UNdeclared sibling is not a neutral omission: every guard written against it
# resolves with existsSync, calls this.skip(), and the gate still prints PASS,
# so the run reports green having exercised none of them. Measured 2026-08-12,
# that gap was 4 guards in the unit tier alone (740 passing / 14 pending against
# a full local checkout's 744 / 10). See test/unit/sibling-coverage.test.js,
# which reports the surface this file leaves uncovered; the same gap applies to
# a sibling that is declared but missing.
#
# ci-dispatch.sh ships each of these at its origin/master (falling back to local
# HEAD) and REFUSES the push if one is not a checkout beside this repo, so a
# declared sibling can never be silently absent.

# The action-suite roster and the anchor-reward, checkpoint and royalty parity
# references.
xchain-documentation
# Checkpoint-commitment parity and the protocol size limits.
xchain-explorer
# Vendored coins-registry byte-identity and the multi-hub federation fixtures.
xchain-hub
# Field roundtrip, the parity harnesses, and the bootstrap fixtures.
xchain-indexer
# The SDK-facing action drills and the seed-contract shape guards.
xchain-sdk
# Consensus-hash conformance and the validator-set parity.
xchain-sync
# The escrow, vesting, crowdsale and amm template drills.
xchain-contracts
# Codec roundtrip, the action-suite count, and CryptoNetworks parity.
xchain-decoder
# The canonical coins registry behind CryptoNetworks parity and the config fixtures.
xchain-encoder
# The SPV seed contract and the protocol size limits.
xchain-vm
# CryptoNetworks getBitcoinJsNetwork parity.
xchain-utxo-tracker
# CryptoNetworks getBitcoinJsNetwork parity.
xchain-regtest-miner
# The gated-send tripwire in the protocol size-limit regression.
xchain-wallet
